WEBVTT

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:39.184
Jane Eyre by Charlotte Bronte We told by Florence Bell Chapter 1 My Story Begins In 1825, I was 10 years old.

00:00:39.204 --> 00:00:51.044
My father and mother were dead.

00:00:51.104 --> 00:01:05.586
I lived with my aunt and uncle, Mr. and Mrs. Reed.

00:01:05.646 --> 00:01:09.306
Their house was called Gates Head Hall.

00:01:09.366 --> 00:01:14.688
The house was in Yorkshire, in the north of England.

00:01:14.748 --> 00:01:24.079
My aunt and uncle Reed had two children, a boy, John, and a girl, Eliza.

00:01:24.139 --> 00:01:28.828
I liked my uncle Reed, and he liked me.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:33.890
But in 1825, my uncle died.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.092
After that, I was very unhappy.

00:01:38.152 --> 00:01:41.163
My aunt Reed did not like me.

00:01:41.223 --> 00:01:46.306
And John and Eliza were unkind to me.

00:01:46.366 --> 00:01:51.608
It was a cold rainy day in December.

00:01:51.668 --> 00:01:54.320
All of us were in the house.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.891
I wanted to be alone.

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:59.164
I wanted to read.

00:01:59.224 --> 00:02:01.378
I opened a book.

00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:05.439
Then I heard my cousin John's voice.

00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:09.871
Jane, Jane Eyre, where are you?

00:02:09.931 --> 00:02:11.742
John shouted.

00:02:11.802 --> 00:02:15.433
He came into the room and he saw me.

00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:18.374
Why are you reading my book?

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:19.804
He asked.

00:02:19.864 --> 00:02:21.645
Give it to me.

00:02:21.705 --> 00:02:23.896
John took the book.

00:02:23.956 --> 00:02:26.147
He hit my head with it.

00:02:26.207 --> 00:02:27.857
I screamed.

00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:29.860
John hit me again.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.853
I pulled his hair, and I kicked him.

00:02:32.912 --> 00:02:35.663
Help, help, mamma!

00:02:35.723 --> 00:02:37.274
John shouted.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:40.094
Jane Eyre is hurting me.

00:02:40.154 --> 00:02:42.695
Aunt Reed ran into the room.

00:02:42.755 --> 00:02:45.185
She pulled me away from John.

00:02:45.245 --> 00:02:48.456
John hit me with a book, I said.

00:02:48.516 --> 00:02:52.317
I hate him, and I hate you too.

00:02:52.377 --> 00:02:55.177
You are a bad girl, Jane.

00:02:55.237 --> 00:02:58.538
My aunt said, why do you hate me?

00:02:58.598 --> 00:03:01.918
You don't like me," I replied.

00:03:01.978 --> 00:03:05.098
John and Eliza are unkind to me.

00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:07.968
I want to leave Gateshead Hall.

00:03:08.028 --> 00:03:10.149
You want to leave?

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:11.819
Aunt Reed said.

00:03:11.879 --> 00:03:13.490
Where will you go?

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.510
Your parents are dead.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.240
You cannot live alone.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.731
Aunt Reed thought for a moment.

00:03:21.791 --> 00:03:28.324
My friend, Mr. Brocklehurst, is the owner of a school, she said.

00:03:28.384 --> 00:03:31.518
I will send you to Mr. Brocklehurst's school.

00:03:31.538 --> 00:03:39.530
A few days later, Mr. Brocklehurst came to Gateshead Hall.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.452
He was a very tall man.

00:03:42.511 --> 00:03:47.023
His eyes were dark and his face was cruel.

00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:54.536
Jane Eyre, he said to me, God does not like bad children.

00:03:54.596 --> 00:03:59.085
God punishes bad children, Jane Eyre.

00:03:59.145 --> 00:04:02.996
God will punish John Reed," I replied.

00:04:03.056 --> 00:04:06.958
John Reed hits me, and he shouts at me.

00:04:07.018 --> 00:04:09.390
That is not true.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:12.292
You are a liar, Jane Eyre.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.424
Mr. Brockle has said.

00:04:14.484 --> 00:04:20.488
You must not tell lies, and you must not live here with your cousins.

00:04:20.548 --> 00:04:23.280
You will come to lowwood school.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.117
You will become a good girl.

00:04:26.176 --> 00:04:29.952
I want to come to your school, sir," I said.

00:04:29.972 --> 00:04:33.144
I want to leave this house.

00:04:33.203 --> 00:04:38.655
Bad girls are punished at my school, Jane Eyre.

00:04:38.715 --> 00:04:40.806
Mr. Brocklehurst said.

00:04:40.866 --> 00:04:44.888
The girls work very hard at Lowwood.

00:04:44.948 --> 00:04:47.268
I will work hard.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:52.616
I will be a good pupil, Mr. Brocklehurst, I said.

00:04:52.676 --> 00:04:56.773
Two weeks later, I left Gateshead Hall.

00:04:56.833 --> 00:05:03.895
I went to Lowwood School.

00:05:03.954 --> 00:05:16.960
Chapter 2 Lowwood School It was the month of January.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.214
I arrived at Lowwood School at night.

00:05:20.274 --> 00:05:24.488
A servant took me up some stairs and into a big bedroom.

00:05:24.508 --> 00:05:27.830
There were many beds in the room.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.172
The girls in the beds were asleep.

00:05:31.232 --> 00:05:34.514
The servant took me to an empty bed.

00:05:34.574 --> 00:05:38.758
I put on my night clothes and I got into bed.

00:05:38.818 --> 00:05:43.140
Soon I was asleep too.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.677
I woke up very early.

00:05:46.736 --> 00:05:49.392
A loud bell was ringing.

00:05:49.452 --> 00:05:52.583
The bedroom was dark and cold.

00:05:52.643 --> 00:05:55.004
I watched the other girls.

00:05:55.064 --> 00:05:59.506
They washed in cold water and they dressed quickly.

00:05:59.566 --> 00:06:03.737
There was a plain brown dress next to my bed.

00:06:03.797 --> 00:06:07.348
And there was a pair of ugly, heavy shoes.

00:06:07.408 --> 00:06:09.509
I washed quickly.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:13.144
Then I put on my new clothes.

00:06:13.203 --> 00:06:15.788
I was very hungry.

00:06:15.848 --> 00:06:19.139
I followed the other girls down the stairs.

00:06:19.199 --> 00:06:23.751
We sat down at long tables in a large dining room.

00:06:23.811 --> 00:06:26.602
Our food was terrible.

00:06:26.662 --> 00:06:29.354
The food is bad again.

00:06:29.414 --> 00:06:33.245
One of the girls said, stand up.

00:06:33.305 --> 00:06:37.256
A teacher shouted, don't talk.

00:06:37.316 --> 00:06:39.228
We stood up.

00:06:39.287 --> 00:06:41.338
We did not speak.

00:06:41.398 --> 00:06:46.410
We walked into a big school room and we sat down.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:52.903
There were about 80 girls in the school room and there were four classes.

00:06:52.962 --> 00:06:56.664
The oldest girls were in the fourth class.

00:06:56.724 --> 00:06:59.676
I was in the first class.

00:06:59.736 --> 00:07:04.738
Four teachers came into the room and we began our lessons.

00:07:04.798 --> 00:07:07.539
The lessons were not interesting.

00:07:07.599 --> 00:07:11.274
First, we read some pages in a book.

00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:16.239
Then, our teacher asked us questions about those pages.

00:07:16.299 --> 00:07:20.471
After four hours, we went outside.

00:07:20.531 --> 00:07:23.062
It was very cold.

00:07:23.122 --> 00:07:26.004
Very soon, a bell rang.

00:07:26.064 --> 00:07:30.706
Lessons started again.

00:07:30.766 --> 00:07:35.398
Three weeks passed.

00:07:35.458 --> 00:07:40.247
One afternoon, the head teacher came into the school room.

00:07:40.307 --> 00:07:43.715
The head teacher's name was Miss Temple.

00:07:43.775 --> 00:07:46.746
Mr. Brocklehurst was with her.

00:07:46.806 --> 00:07:48.998
We all stood up.

00:07:49.058 --> 00:07:51.898
I stood behind an older girl.

00:07:51.958 --> 00:07:55.691
I did not want Mr. Brocklehurst to see me.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:08:00.082
Mr. Brocklehurst walked slowly round the room.

00:08:00.142 --> 00:08:02.963
Everybody was very quiet.

00:08:03.023 --> 00:08:06.574
And then I dropped my book.

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:09.860
Mr. Brocklehurst stopped walking.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.856
He looked at me.

00:08:11.915 --> 00:08:16.048
Ah, the new girl, he said.

00:08:16.107 --> 00:08:19.430
Come here, Jane Eyre!

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:23.642
Then he pointed at two of the older girls.

00:08:23.702 --> 00:08:30.855
You two girls, put Jane Eyre on that high chair, he said.

00:08:30.914 --> 00:08:33.816
Look at Jane Eyre, everybody!

00:08:33.836 --> 00:08:36.380
Mr. Brocklehurst said.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.764
This child is bad.

00:08:38.823 --> 00:08:40.534
She is a liar.

00:08:40.594 --> 00:08:42.424
She will be punished.

00:08:42.484 --> 00:08:50.046
Miss Temple, teachers, girls, do not talk to this child."

00:08:50.106 --> 00:08:52.847
Then he spoke to me again.

00:08:52.867 --> 00:09:00.059
"'Jane Er, you must stand on that chair for two hours,' he said.

00:09:00.119 --> 00:09:03.151
You are a bad girl."

00:09:03.211 --> 00:09:07.586
That evening, I cried and cried.

00:09:07.646 --> 00:09:11.119
But Miss Temple was kind to me.

00:09:11.179 --> 00:09:15.174
You are a good pupil, Jane, she said.

00:09:15.234 --> 00:09:17.696
And you are not a bad girl.

00:09:17.756 --> 00:09:20.740
I am your friend, Jane.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:25.242
Thank you, Miss Temple, I said.

00:09:25.302 --> 00:09:29.774
Loward school was in an unhealthy place.

00:09:29.834 --> 00:09:32.887
The buildings were wet and cold.

00:09:32.946 --> 00:09:35.928
Mr. Brocklehurst owned the school.

00:09:35.988 --> 00:09:37.600
He was a rich man.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:41.574
But he did not buy warm clothes for us.

00:09:41.634 --> 00:09:44.686
And he did not buy good food for us.

00:09:44.746 --> 00:09:47.608
Everybody hated him.

00:09:47.668 --> 00:09:52.432
In the spring, many of the girls became sick.

00:09:52.492 --> 00:09:55.043
Some of them left the school.

00:09:55.103 --> 00:09:57.572
They never came back.

00:09:57.632 --> 00:10:00.573
Many of the girls died.

00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:04.114
That spring was a terrible time.

00:10:04.174 --> 00:10:06.324
We had no lessons.

00:10:06.384 --> 00:10:10.955
Miss Temple and the other teachers took care of the sick pupils.

00:10:11.015 --> 00:10:18.426
Mr. Brocklehurst had to buy better food for us, and he had to buy warm clothes for us.

00:10:18.486 --> 00:10:22.848
Mr. Brocklehurst never came to the school.

00:10:22.908 --> 00:10:28.299
The next year, Loward School moved to a better place.

00:10:28.359 --> 00:10:30.630
It was a healthier place.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:36.701
There were new schoolrooms, new bedrooms, and a new dining room.

00:10:36.761 --> 00:10:40.002
The new buildings were bright and clean.

00:10:40.062 --> 00:10:42.372
The teachers were happy.

00:10:42.432 --> 00:10:47.254
After that, I was happy at Loward School too.

00:10:47.314 --> 00:10:51.694
I was a pupil at Loward School for six years.

00:10:51.754 --> 00:10:54.616
Then, I became a teacher.

00:10:54.676 --> 00:11:04.848
I was a teacher at the school for two years, but I never returned to Gateshead Hall, and the reeds never wrote to me.

00:11:04.908 --> 00:11:25.853
Chapter 3 Thornfield Hall In 1833, I was 18 years old.

00:11:25.913 --> 00:11:30.284
In the summer, Miss Temple left Lowwood School.

00:11:30.344 --> 00:11:32.375
She got married.

00:11:32.435 --> 00:11:35.206
I wanted to leave Lowwood too.

00:11:35.266 --> 00:11:37.966
I wanted a new life.

00:11:38.026 --> 00:11:42.157
I will be a governess, I thought.

00:11:42.217 --> 00:11:47.015
I put an advertisement in a newspaper.

00:11:47.075 --> 00:11:52.746
October 1833, Lowwood.

00:11:52.806 --> 00:11:59.110
A young woman wants to teach one or two children in their home.

00:11:59.171 --> 00:12:11.949
She teaches English, arithmetic, geography, religion, French, drawing and music, J.E.

00:12:12.009 --> 00:12:15.848
I had a reply to my advertisement.

00:12:15.908 --> 00:12:22.857
The reply was from Mrs Fairfax of Thornfield Hall near Milcott.

00:12:22.917 --> 00:12:27.699
Milcott was about 70 miles from Lowwood School.

00:12:27.759 --> 00:12:32.260
Mrs Fairfax wanted a governess for a little girl.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:35.892
I wrote to Mrs Fairfax immediately.

00:12:35.952 --> 00:12:44.858
I was going to be a governess at Thornfield Hall I traveled to Milcott in a coach.

00:12:44.918 --> 00:12:48.340
At Milcott, a servant met me.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.522
He took me to Thornfield Hall.

00:12:51.582 --> 00:12:56.005
At Thornfield Hall, another servant opened the door.

00:12:56.065 --> 00:12:58.026
She was smiling.

00:12:58.086 --> 00:13:01.048
She took me into a small, warm room.

00:13:01.068 --> 00:13:03.990
A lady was in the room.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.072
She was sitting by the fire.

00:13:07.132 --> 00:13:10.344
Are you Mrs. Fairfax?

00:13:10.404 --> 00:13:12.176
I asked her.

00:13:12.236 --> 00:13:18.424
Yes, my dear," she said, and you are Miss Eyre.

00:13:18.484 --> 00:13:20.246
Are you cold?

00:13:20.306 --> 00:13:22.668
Sit by the fire, Miss Eyre.

00:13:22.728 --> 00:13:25.831
A servant will bring you some food.

00:13:25.891 --> 00:13:29.194
Mrs Fairfax is very kind.

00:13:29.254 --> 00:13:33.906
I said to myself, I will be happy here.

00:13:33.966 --> 00:13:37.565
Will I see Miss Fairfax tonight?"

00:13:37.625 --> 00:13:39.216
I asked.

00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:42.046
Mrs. Fairfax looked at me.

00:13:42.106 --> 00:13:44.228
She smiled.

00:13:44.288 --> 00:13:49.930
Mrs. Fairfax, no, no, she said.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:53.670
Your pupil's name is not Miss Fairfax.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:57.772
Your pupil is Adele Barone.

00:13:57.832 --> 00:14:00.813
Adele's mother was a French woman.

00:14:00.873 --> 00:14:03.794
Adele is Mr. Rochester's ward.

00:14:03.854 --> 00:14:06.206
He takes care of her.

00:14:06.266 --> 00:14:08.767
Mr. Rochester?

00:14:08.826 --> 00:14:11.137
Who is Mr. Rochester?

00:14:11.198 --> 00:14:12.948
I asked.

00:14:13.008 --> 00:14:18.341
Mr. Edward Rochester is the owner of Thornfield Hall.

00:14:18.401 --> 00:14:22.713
Mrs. Fairfax said, I am his housekeeper.

00:14:22.773 --> 00:14:25.724
I take care of Thornfield Hall.

00:14:25.784 --> 00:14:28.997
Mr. Rochester is not here now.

00:14:29.057 --> 00:14:31.779
He does not like this house.

00:14:31.839 --> 00:14:33.999
He is often away from home.

00:14:34.019 --> 00:14:38.171
I was very tired.

00:14:38.231 --> 00:14:41.842
Mrs Fairfax took me up the wide stairs.

00:14:41.902 --> 00:14:43.542
She took me to my room.

00:14:43.562 --> 00:14:50.090
I went to bed immediately and I slept well.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:54.750
The next morning I woke early.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:57.092
The sun was shining.

00:14:57.152 --> 00:15:00.174
I put on a plain black dress.

00:15:00.234 --> 00:15:03.017
I opened my bedroom door.

00:15:03.077 --> 00:15:07.752
I walked along a corridor and down the wide stairs.

00:15:07.812 --> 00:15:11.334
I walked out into the sunny garden.

00:15:11.394 --> 00:15:16.324
I turned and I looked up at my new home.

00:15:16.384 --> 00:15:21.784
Thornfield Hall was a beautiful house with many large windows.

00:15:21.844 --> 00:15:25.647
The garden was beautiful, too.

00:15:25.707 --> 00:15:31.041
After a few minutes, Mrs. Fairfax came into the garden.

00:15:31.101 --> 00:15:33.262
She spoke to me.

00:15:33.322 --> 00:15:35.905
Good morning, Miss Eyre.

00:15:35.965 --> 00:15:39.388
She said, You have woken early.

00:15:39.448 --> 00:15:41.717
Mr. Delhi is here.

00:15:41.777 --> 00:15:45.808
After breakfast, you must take her to the schoolroom.

00:15:45.868 --> 00:15:48.910
She must begin her lessons.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:52.432
A pretty little girl walked towards me.

00:15:52.492 --> 00:15:55.134
She was about eight years old.

00:15:55.195 --> 00:16:00.088
She spoke to me in French, and I replied in French.

00:16:00.148 --> 00:16:04.522
After breakfast, I took Adele to the schoolroom.

00:16:04.582 --> 00:16:06.804
We worked all morning.

00:16:06.864 --> 00:16:11.712
Adele enjoyed her lessons, and I was happy.

00:16:11.772 --> 00:16:18.801
In the afternoon, Mrs. Fairfax took me into all the rooms of Thornfield Hall.

00:16:18.862 --> 00:16:23.373
We looked at the paintings and at the beautiful furniture.

00:16:23.433 --> 00:16:26.454
We walked along the corridors.

00:16:26.514 --> 00:16:31.526
Come up onto the roof, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:16:31.586 --> 00:16:36.545
You will see the beautiful countryside around Thornfield Hall.

00:16:36.605 --> 00:16:39.653
We walked up many stairs.

00:16:39.713 --> 00:16:43.534
At last we were at the top of the house.

00:16:43.594 --> 00:16:46.625
We walked along the top corridor.

00:16:46.685 --> 00:16:52.297
Mrs. Fairfax opened a small door and we walked onto the roof.

00:16:52.357 --> 00:16:56.618
Look, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:16:56.678 --> 00:17:00.020
You can see for many miles.

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.481
We stood on the roof for a few minutes.

00:17:03.541 --> 00:17:06.617
Then we went back into the house.

00:17:06.677 --> 00:17:09.794
We walked carefully towards the stairs.

00:17:09.854 --> 00:17:13.386
The top corridor was narrow and dark.

00:17:13.446 --> 00:17:18.118
Suddenly I heard a strange laugh.

00:17:18.178 --> 00:17:21.539
Who is that, Mrs. Fairfax?

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.290
I asked.

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:26.152
Mrs. Fairfax did not reply.

00:17:26.212 --> 00:17:28.163
She knocked on a door.

00:17:28.223 --> 00:17:30.864
Grace, she said.

00:17:30.924 --> 00:17:32.746
The door opened.

00:17:32.806 --> 00:17:35.576
Behind the door was a small room.

00:17:35.636 --> 00:17:38.576
A servant was standing at the door.

00:17:38.636 --> 00:17:41.738
Be quiet, Grace, please!

00:17:41.798 --> 00:17:43.978
Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:17:44.038 --> 00:17:46.990
The woman looked at Mrs. Fairfax.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.682
Then she closed the door.

00:17:49.742 --> 00:17:55.044
That was Grace Poole, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:17:55.104 --> 00:17:57.275
She works up here.

00:17:57.335 --> 00:18:01.977
Sometimes she laughs and talks with the other servants.

00:18:02.037 --> 00:18:04.744
Don't worry about Grace.

00:18:04.804 --> 00:18:17.244
Please come downstairs now, Miss Air.

00:18:17.304 --> 00:18:27.158
Chapter 4 Mr. Rochester Three months passed.

00:18:27.218 --> 00:18:30.719
I had not met the owner of Thornfield Hall.

00:18:30.779 --> 00:18:34.046
Mr. Rochester had not come home.

00:18:34.106 --> 00:18:40.246
One January afternoon, I went out and I walked towards the road.

00:18:40.306 --> 00:18:43.178
I was going to the village of Hay.

00:18:43.238 --> 00:18:46.519
I was going to post a letter in the village.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:50.731
Hay was two miles from Thornfield Hall.

00:18:50.792 --> 00:18:54.634
The day was fine but it was very cold.

00:18:54.694 --> 00:18:59.018
I walked quickly and soon I was near the village.

00:18:59.078 --> 00:19:04.042
Suddenly, A big black and white dog ran past me.

00:19:04.102 --> 00:19:08.694
A moment later, a man on a black horse followed the dog.

00:19:08.754 --> 00:19:12.126
Then I heard an angry shout.

00:19:12.186 --> 00:19:14.758
The dog ran past me again.

00:19:14.818 --> 00:19:17.049
It was barking loudly.

00:19:17.109 --> 00:19:19.090
I turned round.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:25.384
The horse had fallen on the icy ground, and the man had fallen from the horse.

00:19:25.444 --> 00:19:28.059
I walked towards them.

00:19:28.119 --> 00:19:30.514
Can I help you, sir?"

00:19:30.574 --> 00:19:32.176
I asked.

00:19:32.236 --> 00:19:34.238
My horse fell.

00:19:34.298 --> 00:19:36.200
I've heard my foot.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:38.302
The man said.

00:19:38.362 --> 00:19:40.454
The horse stood up.

00:19:40.514 --> 00:19:43.126
The man tried to stand up too.

00:19:43.186 --> 00:19:45.408
But he could not stand.

00:19:45.468 --> 00:19:47.450
He fell onto the ground again.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:52.516
The man was about thirty-five years old.

00:19:52.576 --> 00:19:54.605
He was not handsome.

00:19:54.665 --> 00:19:57.096
But he had a strong face.

00:19:57.156 --> 00:20:00.708
He had dark eyes and black hair.

00:20:00.768 --> 00:20:05.634
He was not very tall, but his body was powerful.

00:20:05.694 --> 00:20:11.564
I'll bring somebody from Thornfield Hall, I said.

00:20:11.624 --> 00:20:14.799
do live at Thornfield?"

00:20:14.859 --> 00:20:16.880
The man asked.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:21.192
I am the governess, I replied.

00:20:21.252 --> 00:20:22.993
Ah, yes.

00:20:23.053 --> 00:20:26.164
The governess, the man said.

00:20:26.224 --> 00:20:28.946
Help me, please.

00:20:29.006 --> 00:20:34.488
The man stood up very slowly, and he put his hand on my shoulder.

00:20:34.548 --> 00:20:37.570
He walked slowly towards his horse.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.281
I helped him.

00:20:39.341 --> 00:20:42.244
He pulled himself onto the horse.

00:20:42.304 --> 00:20:44.008
Thank you.

00:20:44.068 --> 00:20:50.602
Now go home quickly," the man said, and he rode away.

00:20:50.662 --> 00:20:55.726
I walked on to the village, and I posted my letter.

00:20:55.786 --> 00:20:59.568
Then I returned to Thornfield Hall.

00:20:59.628 --> 00:21:03.110
Bright lights were shining in the big house.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:05.472
I went inside.

00:21:05.532 --> 00:21:09.524
A big, black and white dog walked towards me.

00:21:09.584 --> 00:21:12.018
It came from the dining room.

00:21:12.078 --> 00:21:15.382
I had seen the dog before.

00:21:15.442 --> 00:21:18.124
Whose dog is that?

00:21:18.184 --> 00:21:20.346
I asked a servant.

00:21:20.406 --> 00:21:25.478
It's Mr. Rochester's dog, the servant replied.

00:21:25.538 --> 00:21:30.490
Mr. Rochester has come home, but he has hurt his butt.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:33.912
His whore spell on some ice.

00:21:33.972 --> 00:21:36.374
I smiled.

00:21:36.434 --> 00:21:40.918
The owner of Thornfield Hall had returned.

00:21:40.978 --> 00:21:46.151
But I did not see Mr Rochester again that day.

00:21:46.211 --> 00:21:50.334
I saw Mr Rochester the next day.

00:21:50.394 --> 00:21:52.965
He sent for me in the evening.

00:21:53.025 --> 00:21:55.206
I put on a clean dress.

00:21:55.266 --> 00:21:58.288
I brushed my hair carefully.

00:21:58.348 --> 00:22:02.460
Mr Rochester was in the large sitting room.

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:05.242
He was sitting in a big chair.

00:22:05.302 --> 00:22:08.706
His right foot was on a small chair.

00:22:08.766 --> 00:22:12.902
Mrs. Fairfax and Adele were sitting with him.

00:22:12.962 --> 00:22:18.066
This is Miss Eyre, sir, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:22:18.126 --> 00:22:20.898
Mr. Rochester looked at me.

00:22:20.958 --> 00:22:23.800
He did not smile.

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:28.644
Sit by the fire, Miss Eyre, he said.

00:22:28.704 --> 00:22:31.336
Where have you come from?

00:22:31.396 --> 00:22:38.557
From Lowood School, I replied, I was there for eight years.

00:22:38.617 --> 00:22:42.536
Eight years, Mr. Rochester said.

00:22:42.596 --> 00:22:44.727
That is a long time.

00:22:44.787 --> 00:22:47.068
Who are your parents?

00:22:47.128 --> 00:22:50.921
I have no parents, sir, I answered.

00:22:50.981 --> 00:22:52.662
They are dead.

00:22:52.722 --> 00:22:55.974
But where is your home, Miss Eyre?

00:22:56.034 --> 00:22:58.235
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:22:58.295 --> 00:23:00.546
I have no home, sir.

00:23:00.606 --> 00:23:04.240
I have no family, I said.

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:07.602
Why did you come to Thornfield Hall?"

00:23:07.662 --> 00:23:10.022
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:23:10.082 --> 00:23:14.424
I wanted to leave Lowwood, sir, I replied.

00:23:14.484 --> 00:23:17.745
I put an advertisement in a newspaper.

00:23:17.805 --> 00:23:21.306
Mrs. Fairfax replied to my advertisement.

00:23:21.366 --> 00:23:25.708
Yes, I did, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:23:25.768 --> 00:23:29.528
Mrs. Air is a good teacher, Mr. Rochester.

00:23:29.588 --> 00:23:33.898
Mr. Rochester smiled for the first time.

00:23:33.958 --> 00:23:38.008
You are very young, Miss Er."

00:23:38.068 --> 00:23:39.499
He said.

00:23:39.559 --> 00:23:43.460
I am 18, sir, I replied.

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:46.562
Mr. Rochester smiled again.

00:23:46.622 --> 00:23:50.514
He did not ask me more questions.

00:23:50.574 --> 00:23:56.746
After that evening, I did not see Mr. Rochester for a few days.

00:23:56.806 --> 00:24:01.300
Then, one night, he sent me again.

00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:05.604
Sit near me, Miss Air," he said.

00:24:05.664 --> 00:24:09.106
Mrs. Fairfax will talk to Adele.

00:24:09.166 --> 00:24:13.677
I sat down quietly, but I did not speak.

00:24:13.737 --> 00:24:16.508
The fire was very bright.

00:24:16.568 --> 00:24:20.159
I saw Mr. Rochester's face clearly.

00:24:20.219 --> 00:24:23.721
I saw his large, dark eyes.

00:24:23.780 --> 00:24:25.811
He was smiling.

00:24:25.871 --> 00:24:28.082
He was happy.

00:24:28.142 --> 00:24:32.590
After a minute, Mr. Rochester spoke.

00:24:32.650 --> 00:24:36.398
Miss Air, he said.

00:24:36.458 --> 00:24:39.888
You are looking at me very carefully.

00:24:39.948 --> 00:24:42.920
Am I a handsome man?

00:24:42.980 --> 00:24:46.412
No, sir, I said.

00:24:46.472 --> 00:24:49.432
You speak the truth, Miss Air.

00:24:49.492 --> 00:24:51.764
Mr. Rochester said.

00:24:51.824 --> 00:24:54.224
Look at me again.

00:24:54.284 --> 00:24:57.396
Am I a kind man?

00:24:57.456 --> 00:25:00.727
No, sir, I said again.

00:25:00.787 --> 00:25:02.874
You are smiling now.

00:25:02.934 --> 00:25:05.942
But you are not always kind."

00:25:06.002 --> 00:25:10.283
That is true, Mr. Rochester replied.

00:25:10.343 --> 00:25:12.884
I have had a difficult life.

00:25:12.944 --> 00:25:15.476
I have met bad people.

00:25:15.536 --> 00:25:19.016
I have been a bad person myself.

00:25:19.076 --> 00:25:23.019
Now Thornfield Hall is my home.

00:25:23.078 --> 00:25:26.030
But I hate this house.

00:25:26.090 --> 00:25:29.321
You are very young, Miss Eyre.

00:25:29.381 --> 00:25:32.062
You cannot understand me.

00:25:32.123 --> 00:25:34.104
You are right.

00:25:34.164 --> 00:25:37.906
I don't understand you, sir," I said.

00:25:37.966 --> 00:25:39.868
I stood up.

00:25:39.928 --> 00:25:41.980
Where are you going?

00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:44.222
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:25:44.282 --> 00:25:45.773
It is late.

00:25:45.833 --> 00:25:47.834
Adele must go to bed.

00:25:47.894 --> 00:25:49.606
I said.

00:25:49.666 --> 00:25:53.488
Are you frightened of me, Miss Eyre?

00:25:53.548 --> 00:25:55.930
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:25:55.990 --> 00:25:59.114
No, sir, I replied.

00:25:59.174 --> 00:26:02.319
But you say strange things, sir.

00:26:02.379 --> 00:26:05.544
Mr. Rochester smiled.

00:26:05.604 --> 00:26:10.576
Take Adele to her bedroom now, Miss Eyre, he said.

00:26:10.636 --> 00:26:14.148
We will talk again tomorrow.

00:26:14.208 --> 00:26:19.520
After that night, we talked together many times.

00:26:19.580 --> 00:26:26.303
Mr. Rochester was an interesting man, but he was a strange man too.

00:26:26.363 --> 00:26:29.658
I often thought about him.

00:26:29.718 --> 00:26:33.523
Why does Mr. Rochester hate Thornfield?

00:26:33.583 --> 00:26:35.394
I asked myself.

00:26:35.454 --> 00:26:38.684
Thornfield Hall is a beautiful place.

00:26:38.744 --> 00:26:41.125
But Mr. Rochester is not happy.

00:26:41.145 --> 00:26:52.418
Chapter 5 Fire It was March.

00:26:52.478 --> 00:27:03.622
One night I was in bed, but I was not asleep.

00:27:03.683 --> 00:27:06.405
The house was quiet.

00:27:06.465 --> 00:27:11.980
Suddenly I heard a sound in the corridor outside my room.

00:27:12.040 --> 00:27:14.081
Who's there?

00:27:14.141 --> 00:27:15.572
I said.

00:27:15.632 --> 00:27:17.744
Nobody answered.

00:27:17.804 --> 00:27:21.727
Then I heard a strange laugh.

00:27:21.787 --> 00:27:27.292
I got out of my bed, and I went quietly to the door.

00:27:27.352 --> 00:27:29.544
I listened.

00:27:29.604 --> 00:27:32.426
I heard another sound.

00:27:32.486 --> 00:27:37.926
Somebody was walking up the stairs to the top corridor.

00:27:37.986 --> 00:27:43.148
Then I heard somebody close a door.

00:27:43.208 --> 00:27:46.178
Was that Grace Poole?

00:27:46.238 --> 00:27:51.970
I said to myself, yes, it was Grace.

00:27:52.030 --> 00:27:54.570
Why was she laughing?

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:58.510
And why is she walking in the house at night?

00:27:58.570 --> 00:28:00.976
Is she mad?

00:28:01.036 --> 00:28:04.692
I must tell Mrs Fairfax about this.

00:28:04.752 --> 00:28:08.072
I will speak to her now.

00:28:08.133 --> 00:28:13.145
I put on some clothes and I opened the door.

00:28:13.205 --> 00:28:16.956
There was a candle on the floor outside my room.

00:28:17.016 --> 00:28:19.628
The candle was burning.

00:28:19.688 --> 00:28:23.150
There was thick smoke in the corridor.

00:28:23.210 --> 00:28:25.730
I went into the corridor.

00:28:25.790 --> 00:28:28.092
I looked around me.

00:28:28.152 --> 00:28:31.986
The door of Mr. Rochester's bedroom was open.

00:28:32.046 --> 00:28:35.569
And the smoke was coming from Mr. Rochester's room.

00:28:35.589 --> 00:28:40.230
I ran into the room.

00:28:40.290 --> 00:28:43.441
Wake up, sir!

00:28:43.501 --> 00:28:46.112
What happened, Jane?

00:28:46.132 --> 00:28:49.463
There was a fire, sir.

00:28:49.523 --> 00:28:52.354
Grace Paul tried to kill you.

00:28:52.414 --> 00:28:54.624
Stay here, Jane.

00:28:54.684 --> 00:28:56.404
Open the window.

00:28:56.464 --> 00:28:59.288
I'll go upstairs.

00:28:59.348 --> 00:29:03.052
I sat in a chair by the window.

00:29:03.112 --> 00:29:05.292
Time passed.

00:29:05.352 --> 00:29:09.244
At last, Mr. Rochester returned.

00:29:09.304 --> 00:29:13.265
Please don't worry, Jane, he said.

00:29:13.325 --> 00:29:20.487
Grace Poole is a strange woman, but she won't hurt anybody tonight.

00:29:20.547 --> 00:29:22.748
I stood up.

00:29:22.808 --> 00:29:26.709
Good night, sir, I said.

00:29:26.769 --> 00:29:29.906
Mr. Rochester held my hand.

00:29:29.966 --> 00:29:33.973
He looked at me, and he smiled.

00:29:34.033 --> 00:29:38.194
Thank you, my dear friend.

00:29:38.254 --> 00:29:43.536
He said, you saved my life tonight, Jane.

00:29:43.596 --> 00:29:46.067
Good night, sir.

00:29:46.127 --> 00:29:48.428
I said again.

00:29:48.488 --> 00:29:51.378
I went back to my bed.

00:29:51.438 --> 00:29:53.699
I was very tired.

00:29:53.759 --> 00:29:57.764
But at first, I could not sleep.

00:29:57.824 --> 00:30:02.338
Suddenly, I understood something.

00:30:02.398 --> 00:30:05.528
I loved Mr. Rochester.

00:30:05.588 --> 00:30:07.949
He had smiled at me.

00:30:08.009 --> 00:30:10.679
He had held my hand.

00:30:10.739 --> 00:30:13.330
Did he love me?

00:30:13.390 --> 00:30:15.580
I did not know.

00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:22.001
But I thought about Mr. Rochester for a long time.

00:30:22.062 --> 00:30:26.621
I did not see Mr. Rochester the next day.

00:30:26.681 --> 00:30:28.501
He did not send for me.

00:30:28.521 --> 00:30:34.914
In the evening, I went down to Mrs. Fairfax's sitting room.

00:30:34.974 --> 00:30:38.646
The housekeeper was looking out of the window.

00:30:38.706 --> 00:30:44.000
The weather has been good today, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:30:44.060 --> 00:30:47.852
Mr. Rochester had a good day for his journey.

00:30:47.912 --> 00:30:49.683
His journey?

00:30:49.743 --> 00:30:50.974
Where has he gone?

00:30:50.994 --> 00:30:53.065
I asked.

00:30:53.125 --> 00:30:55.358
I was surprised.

00:30:55.418 --> 00:30:58.502
He has gone to Ingram Park.

00:30:58.562 --> 00:31:00.846
Mrs. Fairfax replied.

00:31:00.906 --> 00:31:04.569
Mr. Rochester will stay there for a week or more.

00:31:04.630 --> 00:31:06.932
He has many friends.

00:31:06.992 --> 00:31:11.296
All his friends will be at Ingram Park this week.

00:31:11.356 --> 00:31:15.300
Will there be any ladies at Ingram Park?

00:31:15.360 --> 00:31:16.962
I asked.

00:31:17.022 --> 00:31:22.956
Yes, Mrs. Fairfax said, there will be many ladies there.

00:31:23.016 --> 00:31:26.128
Miss Blanche Ingram will be there.

00:31:26.188 --> 00:31:30.090
Mr. Rochester has known her for many years.

00:31:30.150 --> 00:31:32.882
Is Miss Ingram beautiful?

00:31:32.942 --> 00:31:34.563
I asked.

00:31:34.623 --> 00:31:39.336
She is very beautiful, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:31:39.396 --> 00:31:42.478
Will Mr. Rochester marry her?

00:31:42.538 --> 00:31:44.228
I asked.

00:31:44.288 --> 00:31:47.203
Mrs. Fairfax smiled.

00:31:47.263 --> 00:31:51.157
I don't know, Miss Eyre," she replied.

00:31:51.217 --> 00:31:52.567
I don't know.

00:31:52.587 --> 00:31:56.998
I was very unhappy.

00:31:57.058 --> 00:31:59.279
I went up to my bedroom.

00:31:59.339 --> 00:32:01.779
I looked in my mirror.

00:32:01.840 --> 00:32:06.150
Jane Eyre, I said to myself.

00:32:06.211 --> 00:32:08.321
You are not pretty.

00:32:08.381 --> 00:32:10.101
And you are poor.

00:32:10.161 --> 00:32:13.140
Mr. Rochester will never marry you.

00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:16.300
He will marry Miss Blanche Ingram.

00:32:16.360 --> 00:32:18.462
She is a rich lady.

00:32:18.522 --> 00:32:20.934
You are a poor governess.

00:32:20.994 --> 00:32:23.776
Forget Mr. Rochester Jane Eyre.

00:32:23.836 --> 00:32:29.981
Forget him.

00:32:30.042 --> 00:32:47.404
Chapter 6 Guests at Thornfield Hall Two weeks later, a letter arrived for Mrs. Fairfax.

00:32:47.464 --> 00:32:53.528
Mr. Rochester will return on Thursday, Mrs. Fairfax said.

00:32:53.588 --> 00:32:56.341
Some of his friends will come here with him.

00:32:56.401 --> 00:33:00.144
There will be many guests at Thornfield Hall.

00:33:00.204 --> 00:33:07.570
On Thursday evening, Mrs. Fairfax, Adele and I were in Adele's bedroom.

00:33:07.630 --> 00:33:11.163
Mrs. Fairfax was looking out of the window.

00:33:11.222 --> 00:33:16.644
The guests are arriving now, Mrs Fairfax said.

00:33:16.704 --> 00:33:20.586
I went to the window and I looked out.

00:33:20.646 --> 00:33:23.167
There were three carriages.

00:33:23.227 --> 00:33:26.098
Two people were riding horses.

00:33:26.158 --> 00:33:30.190
Mr Rochester was riding his big black horse.

00:33:30.250 --> 00:33:34.301
A beautiful young woman was riding a white horse.

00:33:34.361 --> 00:33:37.970
Mrs Fairfax pointed to the young woman.

00:33:38.030 --> 00:33:42.278
That is Miss Ingram, the housekeeper said.

00:33:42.338 --> 00:33:44.918
Then she went downstairs.

00:33:44.979 --> 00:33:48.580
Adele wanted to go downstairs too.

00:33:48.640 --> 00:33:52.170
No, Adele, I said.

00:33:52.230 --> 00:33:54.881
We cannot go downstairs tonight.

00:33:54.941 --> 00:33:58.742
Mr. Rochester is talking to his guests.

00:33:58.802 --> 00:34:04.440
The next day, Mrs. Fairfax came into the school room.

00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:10.779
Mr. Rochester wants you to meet his guests tonight, Miss Eyre," she said.

00:34:10.799 --> 00:34:14.120
A doll must meet them too.

00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:19.364
Later, a doll and I went quietly into the sitting room.

00:34:19.424 --> 00:34:23.696
And soon eight ladies came into the room.

00:34:23.756 --> 00:34:28.108
One of them was tall, dark and very beautiful.

00:34:28.168 --> 00:34:30.189
She was Blanche Ingram.

00:34:30.209 --> 00:34:34.128
A doll ran towards her.

00:34:34.188 --> 00:34:40.288
Good evening, beautiful lady," she said in French.

00:34:40.348 --> 00:34:42.910
What a pretty little gal!

00:34:42.971 --> 00:34:45.041
Blanche Ingram said.

00:34:45.102 --> 00:34:53.448
Miss Ingram spoke to the other ladies, and she spoke to Adal, but she did not speak to me.

00:34:53.508 --> 00:34:58.851
Half an hour later, the gentleman came into the room.

00:34:58.912 --> 00:35:01.504
I looked at Mr. Rochester.

00:35:01.564 --> 00:35:06.023
He saw me, but he did not speak to me.

00:35:06.083 --> 00:35:09.592
Miss Ingram pointed at Adele.

00:35:09.652 --> 00:35:14.976
Why doesn't this little girl live at school, Mr. Rochester?

00:35:15.036 --> 00:35:16.818
She asked.

00:35:16.879 --> 00:35:19.931
Adele learns her lessons at home.

00:35:19.991 --> 00:35:22.022
Mr. Rochester replied.

00:35:22.082 --> 00:35:24.114
She has a governess.

00:35:24.174 --> 00:35:25.806
Oh, yes.

00:35:25.866 --> 00:35:30.650
That small woman by the window, Miss Ingram said.

00:35:30.710 --> 00:35:33.038
I had many governesses.

00:35:33.098 --> 00:35:34.795
I hated all of them.

00:35:34.855 --> 00:35:38.236
They were all ugly and stupid.

00:35:38.296 --> 00:35:44.648
Later, Miss Ingram and Mr. Rochester sang some songs together.

00:35:44.708 --> 00:35:47.908
Mr. Rochester had a fine voice.

00:35:47.968 --> 00:35:50.329
I listened to the songs.

00:35:50.389 --> 00:35:52.730
Then I left the room.

00:35:52.790 --> 00:35:55.926
Mr. Rochester followed me.

00:35:55.986 --> 00:35:58.724
What is wrong, Jane?"

00:35:58.784 --> 00:36:00.475
He asked.

00:36:00.535 --> 00:36:04.238
Nothing is wrong, sir, I said.

00:36:04.298 --> 00:36:05.759
But I am tired.

00:36:05.779 --> 00:36:08.522
I am going to my room.

00:36:08.582 --> 00:36:11.074
Good night, sir.

00:36:11.134 --> 00:36:13.656
You are tired.

00:36:13.716 --> 00:36:19.140
And you are unhappy too, Mr. Rochester replied.

00:36:19.200 --> 00:36:22.183
There are tears in your eyes.

00:36:22.243 --> 00:36:25.282
Rest now, Jane.

00:36:25.342 --> 00:36:30.121
But please come and meet my guests tomorrow evening.

00:36:30.182 --> 00:36:32.482
Don't forget my...

00:36:32.542 --> 00:36:35.925
Don't forget, Jane.

00:36:35.985 --> 00:36:41.090
The guests stayed at Thornfield Hall for two weeks.

00:36:41.150 --> 00:36:45.682
Every evening, I went to the sitting room with a dowel.

00:36:45.742 --> 00:36:48.094
Nobody spoke to me.

00:36:48.154 --> 00:36:52.438
Mr. Rochester and Miss Ingram were always together.

00:36:52.498 --> 00:36:57.422
One afternoon, Mr. Rochester went to Milcott.

00:36:57.482 --> 00:37:00.192
He returned late in the evening.

00:37:00.252 --> 00:37:03.123
I met him at the front door.

00:37:03.184 --> 00:37:07.955
Another guest has arrived, sir, I told him.

00:37:08.015 --> 00:37:10.256
His name is Mr. Mason.

00:37:10.316 --> 00:37:13.376
He has come from the West Indies.

00:37:13.436 --> 00:37:18.058
Suddenly, Mr. Rochester's face was pale.

00:37:18.118 --> 00:37:21.230
He held my hand tightly.

00:37:21.290 --> 00:37:23.193
Mason?

00:37:23.253 --> 00:37:25.347
The West Indies.

00:37:25.407 --> 00:37:26.888
Mason.

00:37:26.948 --> 00:37:28.579
He said.

00:37:28.639 --> 00:37:30.780
Are you ill, sir?

00:37:30.841 --> 00:37:32.622
I asked.

00:37:32.682 --> 00:37:34.312
Jane.

00:37:34.372 --> 00:37:36.234
My little friend.

00:37:36.294 --> 00:37:38.095
I've had a shock.

00:37:38.155 --> 00:37:39.516
He said.

00:37:39.576 --> 00:37:43.098
Bring me a glass of wine, please.

00:37:43.158 --> 00:37:46.140
I went quickly to the dining room.

00:37:46.200 --> 00:37:51.759
I returned with a glass of wine, and I gave it to Mr. Rochester.

00:37:51.819 --> 00:37:54.876
What are my guests doing?"

00:37:54.937 --> 00:37:56.547
he asked.

00:37:56.608 --> 00:38:01.010
They are eating and laughing, sir, I replied.

00:38:01.071 --> 00:38:04.862
Mr. Mason is talking to the other guests.

00:38:04.922 --> 00:38:09.386
One day they will all hate me.

00:38:09.446 --> 00:38:11.886
Mr. Rochester said.

00:38:11.946 --> 00:38:14.968
Now go into the dining room again.

00:38:15.028 --> 00:38:18.862
Tell Mason to meet me in the library.

00:38:18.922 --> 00:38:22.210
I gave Mr. Mason the message.

00:38:22.270 --> 00:38:24.978
Then I went to my bedroom.

00:38:25.038 --> 00:38:27.640
I got into my bed.

00:38:27.700 --> 00:38:33.574
Later, I heard Mr. Rochester coming up the stairs with Mr. Mason.

00:38:33.634 --> 00:38:36.686
They were laughing and talking.

00:38:36.746 --> 00:38:46.313
Soon, I was asleep.

00:38:46.374 --> 00:38:55.872
A terrible night.

00:38:55.932 --> 00:39:00.655
Some hours later, I woke up.

00:39:00.715 --> 00:39:03.667
A terrible cry had woken me.

00:39:03.727 --> 00:39:05.918
The moon was bright.

00:39:05.978 --> 00:39:09.180
Its light was shining through my window.

00:39:09.240 --> 00:39:11.121
I listened.

00:39:11.182 --> 00:39:15.945
Then I heard somebody shouting, help!

00:39:16.005 --> 00:39:17.005
Help!

00:39:17.066 --> 00:39:18.456
Rochester!

00:39:18.516 --> 00:39:20.278
Help me!

00:39:20.338 --> 00:39:26.734
The voice came from the Help!

00:39:26.794 --> 00:39:31.728
I got out of bed, and I put an address and some shoes.

00:39:31.788 --> 00:39:33.890
I opened my door.

00:39:33.950 --> 00:39:38.254
All the guests were in the corridor outside the bedrooms.

00:39:38.314 --> 00:39:40.866
They were all asking questions.

00:39:40.926 --> 00:39:42.518
What happened?

00:39:42.578 --> 00:39:45.090
They asked, is there a fire?

00:39:45.150 --> 00:39:46.362
Who is hurt?

00:39:46.422 --> 00:39:48.656
Where is Mr. Rochester?

00:39:48.716 --> 00:39:52.408
I am here," Mr. Rochester said.

00:39:52.468 --> 00:39:56.189
He was walking down the stairs from the top corridor.

00:39:56.249 --> 00:39:59.120
What is wrong, Mr. Rochester?

00:39:59.180 --> 00:40:01.070
Miss Ingram asked.

00:40:01.130 --> 00:40:03.140
What has happened?

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:05.401
Nothing is wrong.

00:40:05.461 --> 00:40:07.721
Mr. Rochester replied.

00:40:07.781 --> 00:40:10.832
One of the servants has had a bad dream.

00:40:10.892 --> 00:40:12.102
Go back to bed.

00:40:12.122 --> 00:40:15.643
I went back to my room.

00:40:15.703 --> 00:40:18.020
But something was wrong.

00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:20.438
I did not get into my bed.

00:40:20.498 --> 00:40:22.179
I waited.

00:40:22.239 --> 00:40:25.700
Soon, somebody knocked on my door.

00:40:25.760 --> 00:40:27.732
I opened the door.

00:40:27.792 --> 00:40:31.204
Mr. Rochester was standing in the corridor.

00:40:31.264 --> 00:40:34.145
Jane, follow me.

00:40:34.205 --> 00:40:36.456
Do not make a sound.

00:40:36.516 --> 00:40:38.908
Mr. Rochester said.

00:40:38.968 --> 00:40:42.110
We went up to the top corridor.

00:40:42.170 --> 00:40:47.779
Mr. Rochester unlocked a door, and we went inside a room.

00:40:47.840 --> 00:40:51.498
Mr. Mason was sitting on a chair in the room.

00:40:51.558 --> 00:40:57.738
His face was pale, and his shirt was covered with blood.

00:40:57.798 --> 00:41:00.979
Then I heard a terrible laugh.

00:41:01.039 --> 00:41:04.240
The sound came from the next room.

00:41:04.300 --> 00:41:08.821
Grace Poole is a mad woman, I thought.

00:41:08.881 --> 00:41:12.671
Why does Mr. Rochester have a mad servant?

00:41:12.731 --> 00:41:17.672
Mr. Rochester spoke quietly to Mr. Mason.

00:41:17.732 --> 00:41:21.474
I am going to bring a doctor, Richard."

00:41:21.534 --> 00:41:23.005
He said.

00:41:23.065 --> 00:41:25.356
Then he spoke to me.

00:41:25.416 --> 00:41:27.737
Stay here, Jane.

00:41:27.797 --> 00:41:30.178
Wash Mr. Mason's arm.

00:41:30.238 --> 00:41:33.400
But do not speak to him.

00:41:33.460 --> 00:41:36.621
Mr. Rochester left the room.

00:41:36.681 --> 00:41:39.412
I washed Mr. Mason's arm.

00:41:39.472 --> 00:41:43.184
We waited for Mr. Rochester and the doctor.

00:41:43.244 --> 00:41:48.830
Mr. Mason did not speak to me, and I did not speak to him.

00:41:48.890 --> 00:41:53.356
After two hours, Mr. Rochester returned.

00:41:53.416 --> 00:41:55.726
The doctor was with him.

00:41:55.786 --> 00:41:59.278
The doctor looked at Mr. Mason's arm.

00:41:59.339 --> 00:42:02.962
She bit me, Mr. Mason said.

00:42:03.022 --> 00:42:04.552
I came up here.

00:42:04.612 --> 00:42:06.304
I wanted to see her.

00:42:06.364 --> 00:42:08.174
I wanted to help her.

00:42:08.234 --> 00:42:10.386
But she bit me.

00:42:10.446 --> 00:42:13.217
Me quiet now, Richard.

00:42:13.278 --> 00:42:16.132
Mr. Rochester said quickly.

00:42:16.192 --> 00:42:19.987
The doctor put a bandage on Mr. Mason's arm.

00:42:20.047 --> 00:42:24.742
Mr. Rochester put Mr. Mason's coat round the injured man's shoulders.

00:42:24.802 --> 00:42:28.025
Then he spoke to me again.

00:42:28.085 --> 00:42:30.768
Run downstairs, Jane.

00:42:30.828 --> 00:42:34.922
Unlock the small door at the side of the house, he said.

00:42:34.982 --> 00:42:37.210
We will follow you.

00:42:37.270 --> 00:42:41.679
I went quickly downstairs, and I opened the door.

00:42:41.740 --> 00:42:46.071
Outside the door, a servant was waiting with the carriage.

00:42:46.131 --> 00:42:49.712
Mr. Mason and the doctor came out of the house.

00:42:49.772 --> 00:42:52.143
They got into the carriage.

00:42:52.203 --> 00:42:56.104
Then Mr. Rochester came out of the house, too.

00:42:56.165 --> 00:43:00.656
Mr. Mason spoke to him through the window of the carriage.

00:43:00.716 --> 00:43:02.546
Help her.

00:43:02.607 --> 00:43:07.350
Be kind to her, Rochester, he said.

00:43:07.410 --> 00:43:11.413
Yes, I will, Mason.

00:43:11.474 --> 00:43:13.804
Mr. Rochester said.

00:43:13.864 --> 00:43:17.726
The servant drove the carriage away.

00:43:17.786 --> 00:43:21.368
Will you walk in the garden with me, Jane?

00:43:21.428 --> 00:43:23.690
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:43:23.750 --> 00:43:26.651
I do not want to sleep now.

00:43:26.711 --> 00:43:30.943
Yes, I will, sir, I said.

00:43:31.003 --> 00:43:34.034
Soon it was morning.

00:43:34.094 --> 00:43:36.775
The birds were beginning to sing.

00:43:36.835 --> 00:43:40.506
The flowers had a sweet smell.

00:43:40.566 --> 00:43:44.288
It has been a strange night, Jane.

00:43:44.348 --> 00:43:48.640
Mr. Rochester said, were you frightened?

00:43:48.700 --> 00:43:52.851
I am frightened of Grace Poole, I said.

00:43:52.911 --> 00:43:55.766
She will hurt you one day.

00:43:55.826 --> 00:43:58.722
I am stronger than she is.

00:43:58.782 --> 00:44:00.684
She will not hurt me.

00:44:00.745 --> 00:44:02.957
Mr. Rochester said.

00:44:03.017 --> 00:44:06.341
He looked at me for a few moments.

00:44:06.401 --> 00:44:09.966
Are you my friend, Jane?

00:44:10.026 --> 00:44:11.687
He asked me.

00:44:11.747 --> 00:44:13.358
Yes, sir.

00:44:13.418 --> 00:44:17.682
I will be your friend forever, I replied.

00:44:17.742 --> 00:44:20.652
Thank you, my dear.

00:44:20.712 --> 00:44:25.126
Mr. Rochester said, I have made mistakes.

00:44:25.187 --> 00:44:27.989
Now I want to be happy.

00:44:28.050 --> 00:44:31.842
That is not wrong, is it, Jane?

00:44:31.902 --> 00:44:34.744
He stopped speaking for a minute.

00:44:34.804 --> 00:44:42.124
Then he said, going to the house, I'll talk to you tomorrow.

00:44:42.184 --> 00:44:47.212
But the next day, I had a letter from Gateshead Hall.

00:44:47.272 --> 00:44:49.474
My aunt reads house.

00:44:49.534 --> 00:44:53.677
The letter was from my cousin Eliza.

00:44:53.737 --> 00:44:56.540
Gateshead Hall.

00:44:56.600 --> 00:44:59.262
Dear Jane Eyre.

00:44:59.322 --> 00:45:03.536
My brother, John, is dead.

00:45:03.596 --> 00:45:06.198
My mother is very ill.

00:45:06.258 --> 00:45:08.770
She wants to speak to you.

00:45:08.830 --> 00:45:11.632
Please come quickly, Jane.

00:45:11.692 --> 00:45:15.484
Your cousin, Eliza Reed.

00:45:15.544 --> 00:45:20.558
I started the journey to my aunt Reed's house immediately.

00:45:20.618 --> 00:45:23.540
I arrived there the next day.

00:45:23.600 --> 00:45:27.332
My aunt Reed was very, very ill.

00:45:27.392 --> 00:45:29.444
She could not move.

00:45:29.504 --> 00:45:32.095
And she did not speak to me.

00:45:32.155 --> 00:45:35.828
I wanted to return to Thornfield Hall.

00:45:35.888 --> 00:45:38.861
I wanted to see Mr. Rochester.

00:45:38.921 --> 00:45:43.916
But Eliza wanted me to stay at Gates Head Hall.

00:45:43.976 --> 00:45:49.681
After three weeks, my aunt spoke to me at last.

00:45:49.742 --> 00:45:53.245
She spoke very slowly.

00:45:53.305 --> 00:45:57.478
Are you Jane Eyre?

00:45:57.538 --> 00:45:59.370
She asked.

00:45:59.430 --> 00:46:04.214
Yes, Aunt Reed, I am Jane Eyre.

00:46:04.274 --> 00:46:06.519
I replied.

00:46:06.579 --> 00:46:12.546
There is a letter for you, Aunt Reed said.

00:46:12.606 --> 00:46:15.308
It is in my desk.

00:46:15.368 --> 00:46:17.989
Cora Eliza, please.

00:46:18.050 --> 00:46:21.142
She will get the letter.

00:46:21.202 --> 00:46:23.944
Eliza came into the room.

00:46:24.004 --> 00:46:28.488
She opened the desk and she gave me a letter.

00:46:28.548 --> 00:46:31.440
Read the letter, Jane.

00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:33.641
My aunt said.

00:46:33.701 --> 00:46:36.673
The letter had come from Madeira.

00:46:36.733 --> 00:46:39.974
but it was three years old.

00:46:40.034 --> 00:46:45.578
Madeira, October 1831.

00:46:45.638 --> 00:46:50.641
Dear Madam, I am Jane Eyre's uncle.

00:46:50.701 --> 00:46:52.482
I am a very rich man.

00:46:52.502 --> 00:46:55.504
I have no children.

00:46:55.564 --> 00:46:59.436
One day Jane will have all my money.

00:46:59.496 --> 00:47:01.487
Tell her about me.

00:47:01.548 --> 00:47:03.799
She must write to me.

00:47:03.859 --> 00:47:06.681
John Eyre.

00:47:06.741 --> 00:47:10.954
I answered that letter.

00:47:11.014 --> 00:47:15.056
Aunt Reed said, I hated you Jane.

00:47:15.076 --> 00:47:19.500
I did not want you to have your uncles money.

00:47:19.560 --> 00:47:22.060
I wrote to John Eyre.

00:47:22.120 --> 00:47:25.963
I wrote Jane Eyre is dead.

00:47:26.023 --> 00:47:29.475
She died at Lowood school.

00:47:29.535 --> 00:47:32.696
I am sorry Jane.

00:47:32.756 --> 00:47:35.775
I was wrong.

00:47:35.836 --> 00:47:39.974
Mrs. Reed died that night.

00:47:40.034 --> 00:47:43.574
I left Gateshead Hall a few days later.

00:47:43.634 --> 00:47:47.036
I took my uncle's letter with me.

00:47:47.096 --> 00:47:51.616
Mr. Rochester met me at Thornfield Hall.

00:47:51.676 --> 00:47:55.707
Welcome back to my house, he said.

00:47:55.767 --> 00:47:58.728
This is your home, Jane.

00:47:58.788 --> 00:48:00.508
Thank you, sir.

00:48:00.569 --> 00:48:04.120
I said, I'm very happy here.

00:48:04.180 --> 00:48:07.620
Mr. Rochester's guests had left.

00:48:07.680 --> 00:48:11.351
No other visitors came to Thornfield Hall.

00:48:11.411 --> 00:48:16.483
Every day Mr. Rochester and I talked together.

00:48:16.543 --> 00:48:21.115
And every day I loved him more.

00:48:21.175 --> 00:48:42.478
Chapter 8 In the Garden In June, the weather was hot.

00:48:42.538 --> 00:48:46.479
One evening, I walked into the garden.

00:48:46.539 --> 00:48:49.980
Mr. Rochester was there, too.

00:48:50.040 --> 00:48:53.241
Do you like this house, Jane?

00:48:53.301 --> 00:48:54.772
He asked.

00:48:54.832 --> 00:48:58.303
Yes, sir, I replied.

00:48:58.362 --> 00:49:02.984
Soon, the Dell will go to live at a school, Jane.

00:49:03.044 --> 00:49:08.234
He said, then, I will not want to govern us here.

00:49:08.294 --> 00:49:10.774
Will you be sad then, Jane?

00:49:10.834 --> 00:49:13.596
Will you leave Thornfield Hall?

00:49:13.656 --> 00:49:16.706
Leave, I said quickly.

00:49:16.766 --> 00:49:19.477
Must I leave Thornfield?

00:49:19.537 --> 00:49:23.908
My dear, Mr. Rochester stopped.

00:49:23.968 --> 00:49:26.500
He was silent for a moment.

00:49:26.560 --> 00:49:31.961
Then he said, I am going to be married soon.

00:49:32.021 --> 00:49:38.332
Oh, sir, I said, then I must go far away.

00:49:38.392 --> 00:49:40.972
Far away from Thornfield.

00:49:41.032 --> 00:49:43.324
Far away from you, sir."

00:49:43.384 --> 00:49:46.056
I started to cry.

00:49:46.116 --> 00:49:49.458
I will always remember you, Jane.

00:49:49.518 --> 00:49:51.440
Mr. Rochester said.

00:49:51.500 --> 00:49:53.661
Will you forget me?

00:49:53.721 --> 00:49:56.593
No, sir, I replied.

00:49:56.653 --> 00:49:58.274
I will never forget you.

00:49:58.294 --> 00:50:01.567
I don't want to leave Thornfield, sir.

00:50:01.627 --> 00:50:03.949
I don't want to leave you.

00:50:04.010 --> 00:50:06.512
Don't leave, Jane.

00:50:06.572 --> 00:50:10.523
Mr. Rochester said, stay here.

00:50:10.583 --> 00:50:12.894
He smiled at me.

00:50:12.954 --> 00:50:16.565
I must not stay here, sir, I said.

00:50:16.626 --> 00:50:19.216
You are going to marry Miss Ingram.

00:50:19.276 --> 00:50:20.967
I am poor.

00:50:21.027 --> 00:50:23.458
I do not have a pretty face.

00:50:23.518 --> 00:50:25.799
But I have a heart.

00:50:25.859 --> 00:50:28.950
It is a loving heart, sir.

00:50:29.010 --> 00:50:33.750
Jane, I am not going to marry Miss Ingram.

00:50:33.810 --> 00:50:36.199
Mr. Rochester said.

00:50:36.259 --> 00:50:38.260
She is rich.

00:50:38.320 --> 00:50:40.200
She is beautiful.

00:50:40.261 --> 00:50:41.921
You are poor.

00:50:41.981 --> 00:50:44.162
You are not beautiful.

00:50:44.222 --> 00:50:47.253
But I want to marry you.

00:50:47.313 --> 00:50:50.824
Will you marry me, Jane?

00:50:50.884 --> 00:50:54.926
For a moment, I could not speak.

00:50:54.986 --> 00:50:58.127
At last, I asked.

00:50:58.187 --> 00:51:01.152
Do you love me, sir?

00:51:01.212 --> 00:51:05.006
I do," he replied.

00:51:05.066 --> 00:51:10.650
Then, sir, I will marry you, I said.

00:51:10.710 --> 00:51:14.170
And Mr. Rochester kissed me.

00:51:14.230 --> 00:51:21.224
My dearest Jane, he said, nothing can stop our marriage now.

00:51:21.284 --> 00:51:24.196
We will be married in a month, Jane.

00:51:24.256 --> 00:51:26.567
We kissed again.

00:51:26.627 --> 00:51:31.374
Then I said good night, and I went into the house.

00:51:31.434 --> 00:51:34.339
I went upstairs to my room.

00:51:34.399 --> 00:51:39.481
Later, I remembered my Uncle John Eyre's letter.

00:51:39.541 --> 00:51:42.382
I will write to him in Madeira.

00:51:42.442 --> 00:51:48.605
I said to myself, I will tell him about my marriage to Mr. Rochester.

00:51:48.665 --> 00:51:50.876
I am very happy.

00:51:50.936 --> 00:51:54.258
My uncle will be happy too.

00:51:54.318 --> 00:51:57.398
Four weeks passed.

00:51:57.458 --> 00:52:01.651
Mr. Rochester was going to buy me many beautiful things.

00:52:01.711 --> 00:52:04.742
He was going to give me many presents.

00:52:04.803 --> 00:52:08.123
But I did not want these things.

00:52:08.183 --> 00:52:11.864
No, Edward, I said.

00:52:11.924 --> 00:52:14.214
I am not beautiful.

00:52:14.274 --> 00:52:17.115
I don't want beautiful things.

00:52:17.175 --> 00:52:21.456
I want you, Edward.

00:52:21.516 --> 00:52:25.086
It was the month of July.

00:52:25.146 --> 00:52:30.808
Two days before our wedding day, Mr. Rochester went away.

00:52:30.868 --> 00:52:34.660
I will return tomorrow," he said.

00:52:34.720 --> 00:52:37.282
I love you, Jane.

00:52:37.342 --> 00:52:41.464
That night I went to my bedroom early.

00:52:41.524 --> 00:52:45.686
My wedding dress and my wedding veil were in my room.

00:52:45.746 --> 00:52:47.886
I looked at them.

00:52:47.946 --> 00:52:54.920
In two days I will beat Jane Rochester, I said to myself.

00:52:54.980 --> 00:52:57.471
Then I went to bed.

00:52:57.531 --> 00:53:00.834
But I did not sleep well.

00:53:00.895 --> 00:53:05.190
The next day, Mr. Rochester returned.

00:53:05.250 --> 00:53:08.062
He looked at me carefully.

00:53:08.122 --> 00:53:10.664
What is wrong, Jane?

00:53:10.724 --> 00:53:11.974
He asked.

00:53:12.034 --> 00:53:14.256
Your face is pale.

00:53:14.316 --> 00:53:16.728
Are you frightened?

00:53:16.788 --> 00:53:22.122
I had a very strange dream last night, I said.

00:53:22.182 --> 00:53:25.464
It was a dream about this house.

00:53:25.524 --> 00:53:30.052
But in my dream, Thornfield Hall had no roof.

00:53:30.112 --> 00:53:32.066
The walls were burnt.

00:53:32.126 --> 00:53:33.888
They were black.

00:53:33.948 --> 00:53:37.450
In my dream, I tried to find you.

00:53:37.510 --> 00:53:40.181
But you were not in the house.

00:53:40.242 --> 00:53:43.514
Are you afraid of a dream, Jane?

00:53:43.574 --> 00:53:46.045
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:53:46.106 --> 00:53:49.898
No, Edward, I replied.

00:53:49.958 --> 00:53:51.910
But I woke up from my dream.

00:53:51.930 --> 00:53:54.552
There was a woman in my room.

00:53:54.612 --> 00:53:57.254
She was tall and heavy.

00:53:57.314 --> 00:53:59.986
She had long black hair.

00:54:00.046 --> 00:54:04.770
The woman was holding a candle, I said.

00:54:04.830 --> 00:54:07.851
She put the candle by my mirror.

00:54:07.912 --> 00:54:13.214
She put my wedging veil over her head, and she looked in the mirror.

00:54:13.274 --> 00:54:16.846
Then I saw her face.

00:54:16.906 --> 00:54:20.987
It was a strange, terrible face, Edward.

00:54:21.048 --> 00:54:27.460
I said, suddenly the woman tore my veil into two pieces.

00:54:27.520 --> 00:54:30.913
She threw the pieces on the floor.

00:54:30.974 --> 00:54:33.986
What happened next?"

00:54:34.047 --> 00:54:36.348
Mr. Rochester asked.

00:54:36.408 --> 00:54:40.132
The woman held her candle near my face.

00:54:40.192 --> 00:54:41.702
I replied.

00:54:41.763 --> 00:54:45.216
She looked at me, and she laughed.

00:54:45.276 --> 00:54:47.978
Then she went away.

00:54:48.038 --> 00:54:51.730
This happened in your dream, Jane.

00:54:51.790 --> 00:54:53.752
Mr. Rochester said.

00:54:53.812 --> 00:54:56.934
He did not happen in my dream, Edward.

00:54:56.994 --> 00:55:02.581
I said, this morning My wedding veil was on the floor of my room.

00:55:02.641 --> 00:55:04.132
It was torn.

00:55:04.192 --> 00:55:06.632
It was in two pieces."

00:55:06.692 --> 00:55:10.744
But the woman did not hurt you, Jane.

00:55:10.804 --> 00:55:12.965
Mr. Rochester said.

00:55:13.025 --> 00:55:16.916
Sleep in a doll's room tonight, my dear.

00:55:16.976 --> 00:55:24.412
You will have no more bad dreams.

00:55:24.472 --> 00:55:38.544
Chapter 9 Mr. Rochester's Wife It was our wedding day.

00:55:38.604 --> 00:55:42.938
We were going to be married in a church near Thornfield Hall.

00:55:42.998 --> 00:55:47.540
After the marriage, we were going to travel to London.

00:55:47.600 --> 00:55:49.732
I got up early.

00:55:49.792 --> 00:55:53.536
I put on my wedding dress and I went downstairs.

00:55:53.596 --> 00:55:56.578
Mr. Rochester was waiting for me.

00:55:56.638 --> 00:56:00.890
At eight o'clock, we walked together to the church.

00:56:00.950 --> 00:56:04.724
The clergyman was standing by the door of the church.

00:56:04.784 --> 00:56:09.467
There were two other people inside the church, two men.

00:56:09.527 --> 00:56:12.129
They were sitting in a dark corner.

00:56:12.189 --> 00:56:14.961
I could not see them very well.

00:56:15.021 --> 00:56:18.163
The clergyman started to speak.

00:56:18.223 --> 00:56:23.286
At every marriage, the clergyman asks an important question.

00:56:23.346 --> 00:56:26.310
He asks the people in the church.

00:56:26.370 --> 00:56:29.812
Is there a problem about this marriage?

00:56:29.872 --> 00:56:33.085
The clergyman spoke loudly.

00:56:33.146 --> 00:56:37.118
He asked this question, and he waited.

00:56:37.178 --> 00:56:40.162
There was silence for a moment.

00:56:40.222 --> 00:56:44.895
And then, one of the men in the dark corner stood up.

00:56:44.956 --> 00:56:47.502
He spoke loudly.

00:56:47.562 --> 00:56:49.889
"'There is a problem.

00:56:49.949 --> 00:56:54.100
These two people must not be married,' he said.

00:56:54.120 --> 00:56:59.522
"'There is not a problem,' Mr. Rochester said to the clergyman.

00:56:59.542 --> 00:57:02.023
"'Please go on with the marriage.'

00:57:02.043 --> 00:57:04.134
"'No.

00:57:04.194 --> 00:57:09.156
I cannot go on with the marriage,' the clergyman replied.

00:57:09.216 --> 00:57:11.227
He spoke to the man in the corner.

00:57:11.247 --> 00:57:15.108
"'What is the problem, sir?'

00:57:15.168 --> 00:57:16.951
he asked.

00:57:17.012 --> 00:57:22.396
Mr. Edward Rochester has a wife.

00:57:22.456 --> 00:57:27.277
Mr. Rochester turned and looked at the man.

00:57:27.338 --> 00:57:29.258
Who are you?

00:57:29.319 --> 00:57:31.549
What do you know about me?

00:57:31.609 --> 00:57:34.010
He asked angrily.

00:57:34.070 --> 00:57:36.961
My name is Briggs, sir.

00:57:37.021 --> 00:57:38.522
I am a lawyer.

00:57:38.582 --> 00:57:43.014
The man replied, I know many things about you.

00:57:43.074 --> 00:57:47.063
Fifteen years ago you were married in the West Indies.

00:57:47.124 --> 00:57:51.274
Your wife's name is Bertha Mason.

00:57:51.334 --> 00:57:53.166
She is alive.

00:57:53.226 --> 00:57:56.929
She lives at Thornfield Hall.

00:57:56.989 --> 00:57:59.701
How do you know that?

00:57:59.761 --> 00:58:02.022
Mr. Rochester shouted.

00:58:02.082 --> 00:58:05.175
The other man in the dark corner stood up.

00:58:05.235 --> 00:58:07.246
He walked towards us.

00:58:07.306 --> 00:58:10.168
It was Richard Mason.

00:58:10.228 --> 00:58:15.118
Bertha Mason is my sister, he said.

00:58:15.178 --> 00:58:18.896
I saw her at Thornfield Hall in April.

00:58:18.956 --> 00:58:22.048
Mr. Rochester's face was pale.

00:58:22.108 --> 00:58:25.500
For a minute, he was silent.

00:58:25.560 --> 00:58:28.991
Then he spoke quietly.

00:58:29.052 --> 00:58:33.144
It is true, he said.

00:58:33.204 --> 00:58:36.766
My wife is living at Thornfield Hall.

00:58:36.826 --> 00:58:38.706
She is mad.

00:58:38.766 --> 00:58:41.348
Come to the house, all of you.

00:58:41.408 --> 00:58:44.030
Come and see Mrs. Rochester.

00:58:44.090 --> 00:58:47.783
Come and see the mad woman!

00:58:47.843 --> 00:58:50.955
We all left the church.

00:58:51.015 --> 00:58:53.576
Nobody spoke.

00:58:53.636 --> 00:58:59.270
At Thornfield, Mrs Fairfax and Adele were waiting for us.

00:58:59.330 --> 00:59:01.972
They were smiling happily.

00:59:02.032 --> 00:59:04.824
Nobody will be happy today.

00:59:04.884 --> 00:59:09.652
Mr Rochester said, We are not married.

00:59:09.712 --> 00:59:16.181
Briggs, Mr. Mason, the clergyman, and I followed Mr. Rochester.

00:59:16.242 --> 00:59:19.164
We followed him up the stairs.

00:59:19.225 --> 00:59:22.216
He took us to the top corridor.

00:59:22.276 --> 00:59:27.181
He unlocked the door, and we went into a small room.

00:59:27.241 --> 00:59:30.484
I had seen this room before.

00:59:30.544 --> 00:59:33.886
We walked through the room to another door.

00:59:33.946 --> 00:59:38.892
Mr. Rochester unlocked this door, and we saw a larger room.

00:59:38.952 --> 00:59:42.186
Grace Poole was sitting in the room.

00:59:42.246 --> 00:59:45.036
But another woman was there too.

00:59:45.096 --> 00:59:47.736
She was tall and heavy.

00:59:47.796 --> 00:59:51.177
Her dark hair was in front of her face.

00:59:51.237 --> 00:59:54.458
The woman turned and looked at us.

00:59:54.518 --> 00:59:58.648
I knew that terrible, mad face.

00:59:58.708 --> 01:00:03.880
I had seen it in my bedroom two nights before.

01:00:03.940 --> 01:00:07.864
The mad woman saw Mr. Rochester.

01:00:07.924 --> 01:00:11.489
She screamed and she ran towards him.

01:00:11.549 --> 01:00:13.619
Be careful, sir.

01:00:13.679 --> 01:00:15.520
Grace Poole said.

01:00:15.580 --> 01:00:18.160
The mad woman was very strong.

01:00:18.220 --> 01:00:21.631
She screamed and she hit Mr. Rochester.

01:00:21.691 --> 01:00:25.722
But Mr. Rochester held her arms.

01:00:25.782 --> 01:00:30.313
This woman is my wife.

01:00:30.373 --> 01:00:32.994
Mr. Rochester said angrily.

01:00:33.054 --> 01:00:35.844
I wanted to forget about her.

01:00:35.904 --> 01:00:38.456
I wanted to marry this young girl.

01:00:38.516 --> 01:00:42.370
Jane Eyre, was I wrong?

01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:45.911
He was silent for a few moments.

01:00:45.972 --> 01:00:49.494
Then he spoke quietly.

01:00:49.554 --> 01:00:55.728
Yes, I was wrong, he said.

01:00:55.788 --> 01:01:00.632
I love Jane Eyre, but I was wrong.

01:01:00.692 --> 01:01:04.204
Now go, all of you.

01:01:04.264 --> 01:01:09.096
I must take care of my mad wife.

01:01:09.156 --> 01:01:13.416
I went slowly downstairs.

01:01:13.476 --> 01:01:18.038
Mr. Briggs, the lawyer, spoke to me.

01:01:18.098 --> 01:01:23.480
I am sorry for you, Miss Eyre, he said.

01:01:23.540 --> 01:01:26.222
You did nothing wrong.

01:01:26.282 --> 01:01:29.933
Your uncle John Eyre is sorry for you too.

01:01:29.993 --> 01:01:32.214
He read your letter.

01:01:32.274 --> 01:01:36.206
And then he met Richard Mason in Madeira.

01:01:36.266 --> 01:01:40.127
Your uncle is dying, Miss Eyre.

01:01:40.188 --> 01:01:43.239
He could not come to England.

01:01:43.299 --> 01:01:45.860
He sent me here.

01:01:45.920 --> 01:01:49.792
He wanted me to stop this marriage.

01:01:49.852 --> 01:01:52.832
I did not answer.

01:01:52.893 --> 01:01:57.084
I went to my room and I locked the door.

01:01:57.145 --> 01:02:00.416
I took off my wedding dress.

01:02:00.476 --> 01:02:04.458
I put on a plain black dress.

01:02:04.518 --> 01:02:08.385
I laid down on my bed.

01:02:08.445 --> 01:02:14.076
I am Jane Eyre today, I thought.

01:02:14.136 --> 01:02:16.507
I will be Jane Eyre tomorrow.

01:02:16.527 --> 01:02:21.051
I will never be Jane Rochester.

01:02:21.111 --> 01:02:24.374
I must leave Thornfield Hall.

01:02:24.434 --> 01:02:27.276
I must never see Mr Rochester again.

01:02:27.296 --> 01:02:31.469
My life here is finished.

01:02:31.530 --> 01:02:36.353
Many hours later, I got off the bed.

01:02:36.414 --> 01:02:38.975
I unlocked my door.

01:02:39.035 --> 01:02:43.568
Mr. Rochester was waiting outside my room.

01:02:43.628 --> 01:02:48.230
You are unhappy, Jane, he said.

01:02:48.290 --> 01:02:51.412
I am very, very sorry.

01:02:51.473 --> 01:02:55.355
Jane, we will leave Thornfield.

01:02:55.416 --> 01:02:57.648
We will go to another country.

01:02:57.708 --> 01:02:59.338
We will be happy again.

01:02:59.358 --> 01:03:02.850
I cannot be your wife.

01:03:02.910 --> 01:03:06.704
I cannot live with you, I said.

01:03:06.764 --> 01:03:09.782
I must leave you, Edward.

01:03:09.842 --> 01:03:12.379
Listen, Jane.

01:03:12.439 --> 01:03:14.850
Mr. Rochester said.

01:03:14.910 --> 01:03:18.902
My father wanted me to marry Bertha Mason.

01:03:18.962 --> 01:03:21.614
Her family was very rich.

01:03:21.674 --> 01:03:23.544
I married her.

01:03:23.604 --> 01:03:26.136
My father was happy.

01:03:26.196 --> 01:03:29.068
But I was not happy.

01:03:29.128 --> 01:03:31.258
Bertha was mad.

01:03:31.319 --> 01:03:33.970
And she was a bad woman.

01:03:34.030 --> 01:03:36.671
Nobody told me about her.

01:03:36.731 --> 01:03:38.701
She was married to me.

01:03:38.761 --> 01:03:41.061
But she met other men.

01:03:41.121 --> 01:03:43.532
She was drunk every day.

01:03:43.592 --> 01:03:47.334
She tried to kill me many times.

01:03:47.394 --> 01:03:53.218
After four years, I brought Bertha here to Thornfield Hall.

01:03:53.278 --> 01:03:55.480
Mr. Rochester said.

01:03:55.540 --> 01:03:58.752
Then I went away.

01:03:58.812 --> 01:04:02.184
Grace Poole took care of Bertha.

01:04:02.244 --> 01:04:04.624
I met other women.

01:04:04.685 --> 01:04:07.489
One of them was a French singer.

01:04:07.550 --> 01:04:09.964
She was Adele's mother.

01:04:10.024 --> 01:04:13.098
Adele is my daughter, Jane.

01:04:13.158 --> 01:04:16.060
But I did not love the French singer.

01:04:16.120 --> 01:04:18.652
I did not love anybody.

01:04:18.712 --> 01:04:22.144
I came home to Thornfield Hall.

01:04:22.205 --> 01:04:26.048
Then you came here and I loved you.

01:04:26.068 --> 01:04:29.970
I will always love you.

01:04:30.031 --> 01:04:33.434
Please stay with me, Jane.

01:04:33.494 --> 01:04:36.862
No, Edward, I said.

01:04:36.922 --> 01:04:38.928
I am going away.

01:04:38.988 --> 01:04:44.330
We will be unhappy, but we must not be together.

01:04:44.390 --> 01:04:47.842
Goodbye, Edward."

01:04:47.902 --> 01:04:49.813
Oh, Jane.

01:04:49.873 --> 01:04:51.874
Jane, my love!

01:04:51.934 --> 01:04:55.355
Mr. Rochester said, don't leave me.

01:04:55.375 --> 01:04:59.306
I kissed Mr. Rochester.

01:04:59.366 --> 01:05:02.158
God will help you, Edward.

01:05:02.218 --> 01:05:04.264
I said.

01:05:04.324 --> 01:05:08.180
Quickly I went into my room.

01:05:08.241 --> 01:05:10.891
I put some clothes into a bag.

01:05:10.952 --> 01:05:15.294
Later I heard Mr. Rochester go into his room.

01:05:15.354 --> 01:05:19.206
Very quietly I went downstairs.

01:05:19.266 --> 01:05:22.958
I opened the small door at the side of the house.

01:05:23.018 --> 01:05:27.989
I left Thornfield Hall and I walked to the road.

01:05:28.050 --> 01:05:30.100
It was dark.

01:05:30.160 --> 01:05:33.754
Soon a coach came along the road.

01:05:33.814 --> 01:05:37.238
I gave all my money to the driver of the coach.

01:05:37.299 --> 01:05:41.250
I got into the coach.

01:05:41.310 --> 01:05:46.724
Many hours later, the coach stopped.

01:05:46.784 --> 01:05:49.635
It was ten o'clock in the morning.

01:05:49.695 --> 01:05:54.748
You must give me more money now, the driver said.

01:05:54.808 --> 01:05:58.290
I have no more money, I said.

01:05:58.350 --> 01:06:03.224
You have no more money, then you must get out of the coach.

01:06:03.284 --> 01:06:05.356
The driver said.

01:06:05.416 --> 01:06:08.116
I got down onto the road.

01:06:08.176 --> 01:06:10.847
The coach moved away quickly.

01:06:10.907 --> 01:06:14.308
But I had left my back in the coach.

01:06:14.368 --> 01:06:16.688
I looked around me.

01:06:16.748 --> 01:06:20.010
I was on a cold, empty moor.

01:06:20.070 --> 01:06:23.110
I was tired and hungry.

01:06:23.170 --> 01:06:25.871
I walked and walked.

01:06:25.931 --> 01:06:27.982
I had no money.

01:06:28.042 --> 01:06:30.292
I had no food.

01:06:30.352 --> 01:06:33.544
I walked until the evening came.

01:06:33.605 --> 01:06:38.029
At last, I lay down on the ground.

01:06:38.089 --> 01:06:40.441
I fell asleep immediately.

01:06:40.461 --> 01:06:53.524
Chapter 10 More House The next morning, I woke late.

01:06:53.585 --> 01:07:03.745
I walked along the road for many miles.

01:07:03.805 --> 01:07:06.166
It started to rain.

01:07:06.226 --> 01:07:09.197
Soon my clothes were wet.

01:07:09.258 --> 01:07:11.438
I saw no one.

01:07:11.498 --> 01:07:14.630
I walked on the moor all day.

01:07:14.690 --> 01:07:18.572
In the evening I was very tired again.

01:07:18.592 --> 01:07:23.484
I must sleep soon, I thought.

01:07:23.544 --> 01:07:25.884
Where shall I sleep?

01:07:25.944 --> 01:07:29.024
Then I saw a light.

01:07:29.084 --> 01:07:31.852
I walked slowly towards it.

01:07:31.912 --> 01:07:34.873
The rain was falling heavily.

01:07:34.934 --> 01:07:38.185
But I saw a house near the road.

01:07:38.245 --> 01:07:40.656
I walked up to the house.

01:07:40.716 --> 01:07:42.848
I knocked on the door.

01:07:42.908 --> 01:07:46.790
I waited, but nobody opened the door.

01:07:46.850 --> 01:07:49.410
I stood outside the house.

01:07:49.471 --> 01:07:53.622
I was very cold and very tired.

01:07:53.682 --> 01:07:56.313
I could not move.

01:07:56.374 --> 01:07:59.616
I am going to die here.

01:07:59.676 --> 01:08:01.258
I said.

01:08:01.319 --> 01:08:05.341
Then I heard a young man's voice.

01:08:05.401 --> 01:08:08.632
The man was standing behind me.

01:08:08.692 --> 01:08:14.196
No, you will not die at more house, the man said.

01:08:14.256 --> 01:08:17.688
Then he unlocked the door of the house.

01:08:17.747 --> 01:08:20.069
He took me into the house.

01:08:20.129 --> 01:08:23.891
He took me into a warm sitting room.

01:08:23.952 --> 01:08:27.660
Please sit down, he said.

01:08:27.720 --> 01:08:30.538
Two pretty young women came into the room.

01:08:30.558 --> 01:08:36.502
"'Give this poor woman some fool, Diana,' the young man said.

01:08:36.522 --> 01:08:39.974
"'Give her some dry clothes, Mary.'

01:08:40.033 --> 01:08:42.085
Then he spoke to me again.

01:08:42.105 --> 01:08:46.447
"'My name is Syngen Rivers,' he said.

01:08:46.467 --> 01:08:50.190
"'These are my sisters, Diana and Mary.

01:08:50.210 --> 01:08:53.151
"'What is your name, young woman?'

01:08:53.171 --> 01:08:56.633
"'My name is Jane.

01:08:56.692 --> 01:08:59.564
Elliot, I said.

01:08:59.623 --> 01:09:02.225
I closed my eyes.

01:09:02.284 --> 01:09:06.366
Jane is very tired, Diana said.

01:09:06.426 --> 01:09:08.988
She must go to bed now.

01:09:09.047 --> 01:09:14.326
I stayed in bed at Morehouse for three days.

01:09:14.386 --> 01:09:18.654
Diana and Mary Rivers were governesses.

01:09:18.714 --> 01:09:22.096
They were staying at Morehouse for a few days.

01:09:22.156 --> 01:09:25.608
Sinjin, their brother, was a clergyman.

01:09:25.668 --> 01:09:28.049
They were very kind to me.

01:09:28.109 --> 01:09:31.861
Soon, we were good friends.

01:09:31.921 --> 01:09:36.924
One day, Sinjin asked me about my life.

01:09:36.984 --> 01:09:41.056
I was a governess too, I told him.

01:09:41.116 --> 01:09:44.262
And I told him about Lowwood School.

01:09:44.322 --> 01:09:48.058
But I did not tell him about Thornfield Hall.

01:09:48.118 --> 01:09:52.020
I did not tell him about Mr. Rochester.

01:09:52.080 --> 01:09:56.082
I want to work, Singin', I said.

01:09:56.142 --> 01:09:58.194
Will you help me?

01:09:58.254 --> 01:10:01.866
I have a plan, Singin', said.

01:10:01.926 --> 01:10:05.208
A few miles from here, there is a village.

01:10:05.268 --> 01:10:08.840
Many of the girls in the village cannot read or write.

01:10:08.900 --> 01:10:12.557
I am going to pay for a girl's school in the village.

01:10:12.617 --> 01:10:16.384
But I must find a teacher for these girls."

01:10:16.445 --> 01:10:18.826
I will teach them, Singen.

01:10:18.886 --> 01:10:22.378
I said, good, he said.

01:10:22.438 --> 01:10:25.380
There will be a small house next to the school.

01:10:25.440 --> 01:10:27.472
You will live there."

01:10:27.532 --> 01:10:32.265
Three days later, a letter arrived for Singen.

01:10:32.325 --> 01:10:40.011
Diana, Mary, our uncle John is dead, he told his sisters.

01:10:40.071 --> 01:10:43.724
But we will not have any of his money."

01:10:43.784 --> 01:10:46.735
He gave the letter to his sisters.

01:10:46.794 --> 01:10:48.506
They read it.

01:10:48.566 --> 01:10:53.187
Uncle John was our muppest brother, Diana told me.

01:10:53.247 --> 01:10:58.570
He was very rich, but he has given all his money to another niece.

01:10:58.630 --> 01:11:01.200
We do not know her.

01:11:01.260 --> 01:11:04.752
Soon I went to live in the village.

01:11:04.812 --> 01:11:07.726
I lived in the house next to the school.

01:11:07.786 --> 01:11:10.790
Every day I taught the girls.

01:11:10.850 --> 01:11:13.320
My pupils worked hard.

01:11:13.380 --> 01:11:15.802
But I was not happy.

01:11:15.862 --> 01:11:20.204
Every day I thought about Edward Rochester.

01:11:20.264 --> 01:11:23.236
Does he think about me?

01:11:23.296 --> 01:11:25.568
I asked myself.

01:11:25.628 --> 01:11:28.459
Four months passed.

01:11:28.519 --> 01:11:32.371
One day, Syngen Rivers came to my house.

01:11:32.431 --> 01:11:34.352
He was holding a letter.

01:11:34.412 --> 01:11:36.422
He was worried.

01:11:36.482 --> 01:11:38.342
What is wrong?"

01:11:38.402 --> 01:11:40.034
I asked.

01:11:40.094 --> 01:11:45.038
I want to ask you three questions, Jane, he replied.

01:11:45.098 --> 01:11:47.850
Is your name Jane Elliott?

01:11:47.910 --> 01:11:50.342
Do you have another name?

01:11:50.402 --> 01:11:53.804
Do you know Jane Eyre?

01:11:53.864 --> 01:11:56.576
I looked at him for a moment.

01:11:56.637 --> 01:11:59.029
I did not speak.

01:11:59.089 --> 01:12:03.712
I have some news for Jane Eyre, Singen said.

01:12:03.772 --> 01:12:08.155
Jane Eyre was a pupil at Lowwood School.

01:12:08.215 --> 01:12:16.800
Then she was a governess at Thornfield Hall, the home of Mr. Edward Rochester.

01:12:16.860 --> 01:12:19.011
How do you know this?

01:12:19.071 --> 01:12:20.332
I asked.

01:12:20.392 --> 01:12:23.184
What do you know about Mr. Rochester?

01:12:23.244 --> 01:12:25.245
How is he?

01:12:25.305 --> 01:12:28.707
I don't know, singin' said.

01:12:28.768 --> 01:12:31.299
This letter is from a lawyer.

01:12:31.359 --> 01:12:34.992
The lawyer tells a story about Mr. Rochester.

01:12:35.052 --> 01:12:42.966
Mr. Rochester had a mad wife, but he tried Thornfield.

01:12:43.026 --> 01:12:48.628
Now, this lawyer, Mr. Briggs, is trying to find her.

01:12:48.688 --> 01:12:53.070
I will tell you the truth, Singen, I said.

01:12:53.130 --> 01:12:56.102
My name is not Jane Elliott.

01:12:56.162 --> 01:12:58.592
My name is Jane Eyre.

01:12:58.652 --> 01:13:02.274
And I was a governor at Thornfield Hall.

01:13:02.334 --> 01:13:05.286
I know Mr. Rochester.

01:13:05.346 --> 01:13:09.628
Did Mr. Briggs write anything about Mr. Rochester?

01:13:09.688 --> 01:13:11.056
No.

01:13:11.116 --> 01:13:14.834
The letter is about you, Jane," Singen said.

01:13:14.894 --> 01:13:17.996
Your uncle, John Eyre, is dead.

01:13:18.056 --> 01:13:21.768
John Eyre has given you twenty thousand pounds.

01:13:21.828 --> 01:13:23.998
You are rich, Jane.

01:13:24.058 --> 01:13:26.980
But why did Mr. Briggs write to you?

01:13:27.000 --> 01:13:28.811
I asked.

01:13:28.871 --> 01:13:32.983
My mother's name was Eyre, Singen said.

01:13:33.043 --> 01:13:35.904
She was your father's sister, Jane.

01:13:35.964 --> 01:13:41.994
Then you, Diana and Mary, are my cousins, I said.

01:13:42.054 --> 01:13:44.523
I thought carefully for a moment.

01:13:44.543 --> 01:13:48.185
"'Right to Diana and Mary,' I said.

01:13:48.205 --> 01:13:50.366
"'They must come home.

01:13:50.386 --> 01:13:54.288
"'I will give all of you some of Uncle John's money.'

01:13:54.308 --> 01:13:59.490
"'The next day I wrote to Mr. Briggs.

01:13:59.510 --> 01:14:05.333
"'I gave Singed Diana and Mary £5,000 each.

01:14:05.353 --> 01:14:08.575
"'I wrote to Mrs. Fairfax too.

01:14:08.595 --> 01:14:12.502
"'But she did not reply.

01:14:12.562 --> 01:14:16.048
Six months passed.

01:14:16.108 --> 01:14:19.460
I heard nothing from Thornfield Hall.

01:14:19.520 --> 01:14:23.171
I heard nothing about Mr. Rochester.

01:14:23.231 --> 01:14:28.843
Then, one day, I was walking on the moor.

01:14:28.903 --> 01:14:32.254
Suddenly, I heard a voice.

01:14:32.314 --> 01:14:34.835
There was nobody on the moor.

01:14:34.895 --> 01:14:37.756
But the voice was calling my name.

01:14:37.816 --> 01:14:39.206
Jane.

01:14:39.266 --> 01:14:40.397
Jane!

01:14:40.457 --> 01:14:42.170
Jane!

01:14:42.229 --> 01:14:47.624
That is Mr. Rochester's voice, I said to myself.

01:14:47.684 --> 01:14:54.376
Then I shouted, I am coming Edward, I am coming!

01:14:54.436 --> 01:14:59.527
I ran to Morehouse, I spoke to my cousins.

01:14:59.587 --> 01:15:04.068
I am going to Thornfield Hall tomorrow, I told them.

01:15:04.128 --> 01:15:11.514
I began my journey the next day.

01:15:11.574 --> 01:15:18.419
Chapter 11.

01:15:18.479 --> 01:15:21.871
My story ends.

01:15:21.931 --> 01:15:26.744
Two days later, I got out of the coach.

01:15:26.804 --> 01:15:30.656
I was standing on the road near Thornfield Hall.

01:15:30.716 --> 01:15:33.238
I ran across the fields.

01:15:33.298 --> 01:15:36.410
Was Mr. Rochester at Thornfield?

01:15:36.470 --> 01:15:38.615
Was he ill?

01:15:38.675 --> 01:15:41.961
And then I saw the house.

01:15:42.021 --> 01:15:44.532
The house had no roof.

01:15:44.592 --> 01:15:47.714
Its walls were burnt and black.

01:15:47.774 --> 01:15:51.024
Nobody was living there.

01:15:51.084 --> 01:15:55.146
I looked at the burnt black house.

01:15:55.206 --> 01:15:57.808
I had seen this before.

01:15:57.868 --> 01:16:00.619
I had seen it in a dream.

01:16:00.679 --> 01:16:02.680
I was frightened.

01:16:02.740 --> 01:16:05.741
Where was Edward Rochester?

01:16:05.801 --> 01:16:08.579
I went to the village of Hay.

01:16:08.639 --> 01:16:11.468
I asked about Thornfield Hall.

01:16:11.528 --> 01:16:14.841
I asked about Mr. Rochester.

01:16:14.901 --> 01:16:20.526
Three months ago, there was a fire at Thornfield Hall.

01:16:20.586 --> 01:16:24.879
A man told me, the madwoman burnt the house.

01:16:24.939 --> 01:16:27.969
She was Mr. Rochester's wife.

01:16:28.029 --> 01:16:30.859
Was Mr. Rochester in the house?"

01:16:30.919 --> 01:16:32.240
I asked.

01:16:32.300 --> 01:16:34.602
Yes, he was there.

01:16:34.622 --> 01:16:36.654
The man replied.

01:16:36.714 --> 01:16:39.456
He tried to save his wife's life.

01:16:39.516 --> 01:16:42.069
He went into the burning house.

01:16:42.129 --> 01:16:45.332
But the mad woman jumped from the roof.

01:16:45.392 --> 01:16:47.463
She died.

01:16:47.522 --> 01:16:50.294
Was Mr. Rochester hurt?"

01:16:50.354 --> 01:16:52.436
I asked quickly.

01:16:52.496 --> 01:16:53.838
Yes.

01:16:53.898 --> 01:16:56.080
He was badly hurt.

01:16:56.140 --> 01:16:57.732
The man said.

01:16:57.792 --> 01:16:59.583
He is blind.

01:16:59.643 --> 01:17:01.394
He can't see.

01:17:01.454 --> 01:17:05.719
And he has only one hand.

01:17:05.779 --> 01:17:07.630
Where is he?

01:17:07.690 --> 01:17:08.882
I asked.

01:17:08.942 --> 01:17:10.846
Where is he?

01:17:10.906 --> 01:17:13.859
He is living at Ferndine.

01:17:13.919 --> 01:17:18.040
It is an old house, about thirty miles away."

01:17:18.100 --> 01:17:19.161
The man said.

01:17:19.181 --> 01:17:21.532
"'Do you have a carriage?'

01:17:21.592 --> 01:17:22.502
I asked.

01:17:22.562 --> 01:17:26.334
I must go to Ferndine immediately."

01:17:26.394 --> 01:17:30.395
I got out of the carriage near Ferndine.

01:17:30.455 --> 01:17:32.446
I walked to the house.

01:17:32.506 --> 01:17:34.586
I knocked on the door.

01:17:34.646 --> 01:17:37.038
A servant opened it.

01:17:37.098 --> 01:17:39.070
I knew her.

01:17:39.130 --> 01:17:42.652
Oh, Miss Eyre, you have come!"

01:17:42.712 --> 01:17:43.792
she said.

01:17:43.852 --> 01:17:46.794
Mr. Rochester has been calling your name.

01:17:46.814 --> 01:17:50.295
A bell rang in another room.

01:17:50.355 --> 01:17:54.156
That is Mr. Rochester's bell, the woman said.

01:17:54.216 --> 01:17:56.648
He wants some candles.

01:17:56.707 --> 01:18:00.459
There were two candles on a table near the door.

01:18:00.519 --> 01:18:04.111
The woman lit them and she picked them up.

01:18:04.171 --> 01:18:12.404
Mr. Rochester is blind, but he always burns candles in his room in the evenings, she said.

01:18:12.464 --> 01:18:16.055
Give the candles to me, I said.

01:18:16.115 --> 01:18:18.566
I'll take them to him.

01:18:18.626 --> 01:18:22.306
I opened the door of Mr. Rochester's room.

01:18:22.366 --> 01:18:25.987
His black and white dog was sitting by the fire.

01:18:26.047 --> 01:18:30.593
The dog jumped up and ran towards me.

01:18:30.653 --> 01:18:33.068
Who is there?

01:18:33.128 --> 01:18:35.760
Mr. Rochester said.

01:18:35.820 --> 01:18:38.421
Don't you know me, Edward?

01:18:38.481 --> 01:18:39.852
I asked.

01:18:39.912 --> 01:18:42.312
Your dog knows me?

01:18:42.372 --> 01:18:45.294
I put the candles on a table.

01:18:45.354 --> 01:18:48.765
I held Mr. Rochester's hand.

01:18:48.825 --> 01:18:54.267
I know that voice, and I know this little hand.

01:18:54.327 --> 01:18:59.890
Mr. Rochester said, is that you, Jane?

01:18:59.950 --> 01:19:01.456
Yes, sir.

01:19:01.516 --> 01:19:05.114
I have found you at last," I said.

01:19:05.174 --> 01:19:07.404
I will never leave you again.

01:19:07.424 --> 01:19:13.056
Then I told Mr. Rochester my story.

01:19:13.116 --> 01:19:16.536
Why did you leave your cousins, Jane?

01:19:16.596 --> 01:19:18.826
Mr. Rochester asked.

01:19:18.886 --> 01:19:21.637
Why did you come back to me?

01:19:21.697 --> 01:19:23.578
I am blind.

01:19:23.638 --> 01:19:25.188
I have only one hand.

01:19:25.208 --> 01:19:30.667
I will take care of you, Edward, I said.

01:19:30.727 --> 01:19:35.778
But I don't want a servant, Mr. Rochester replied.

01:19:35.838 --> 01:19:38.160
I want a wife.

01:19:38.220 --> 01:19:42.454
You will have a wife, Edward, I said.

01:19:42.514 --> 01:19:44.686
I will be your wife.

01:19:44.746 --> 01:19:46.858
I will marry you.

01:19:46.918 --> 01:19:50.660
I loved you very much at Thornfield Hall.

01:19:50.720 --> 01:19:54.874
Now, I love you more.

01:19:54.934 --> 01:19:59.056
Mr. Rochester and I got married.

01:19:59.116 --> 01:20:02.966
After a time, his eyes were better.

01:20:03.026 --> 01:20:05.408
He could see a little.

01:20:05.468 --> 01:20:09.662
He saw the face of our first child.

01:20:09.722 --> 01:20:18.320
My dear Edward and I are very happy.

01:20:18.380 --> 01:20:22.765
.

01:20:22.825 --> 01:20:22.865
.

